    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"commitment to sustainability\" thing feels a bit like a cop-out. if we do that, the people calling us out on twitter are just gonna say we're virtue signaling without actually backing the policy. if you're being honest, isn't it basically inevitable that we have to pick a side to keep our brand relevance in a few years? like, is \"neutrality\" even a viable long-term business strategy anymore?",
